        <li id="note-5">The eight funds’ own latest reports, summed by us: CPP Investments $793.3B (31 Mar 2026, note 3); La Caisse $517.3B, with its Port of Brisbane, TransGrid, Eurostar, Sizewell C and REM holdings (31 Dec 2025, <a href="https://www.lacaisse.com/sites/default/files/medias/pdf/en/ra/2025_lacaisse_annual_report.pdf">annual report</a>); Ontario Teachers’ $279.4B, its five European airports and about $100 billion in Canada (<a href="https://www.otpp.com/content/dam/otpp/documents/reports/2025-ar/otpp-2025-annual-report-eng.pdf">annual report</a>; <a href="https://www.cantechletter.com/newswires/ontario-teachers-sets-objective-to-invest-an-additional-10-billion-in-canada-by-the-end-of-2027/">release</a>); PSP $320.6B (31 Mar 2026, <a href="https://www.investpsp.com/en/news/psp-investments-outperforms-10-year-benchmarks-and-posts-solid-performance-in-fiscal-2026">release</a>); BCI $265.4B net, $36.5B infrastructure and its West Coast holdings (31 Mar 2026, <a href="https://www.bci.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/2026-About-BCI-2P-General-Secured.pdf">fact sheet</a>); AIMCo $194.7B under management, 40.2% in Canada (<a href="https://2025.annualreports.aimco.ca/">annual report</a>); OMERS $145.2B (<a href="https://www.omers.com/news/omers-earns-8-2-billion-in-net-investment-income-in-2025">release</a>); HOOPP $131.9B, about 49% in Canada (<a href="https://hoopp.com/docs/default-source/investments-library/annual-reports/hoopp-2025-annual-report.pdf">annual report</a>). The year-ends fall three months apart and BCI, AIMCo and La Caisse also manage non-pension money, so the total is given as about $2.6 trillion.</li>
        <li id="note-6">MSCI ACWI Index factsheet, 30 September 2026: Canada 2.9%. <a href="https://www.msci.com/documents/10199/8d97d244-4685-4200-a24c-3e2942e3adeb">msci.com</a></li>
        <li id="note-7">The Canadian Press via CP24, “CPP Investments and OMERS selling Associated British Ports stakes to IFM Investors,” 21 October 2026: CPP 33.9%, OMERS 30.0%; IFM is owned by Australian pension funds. <a href="https://www.cp24.com/news/money/2026/10/21/cpp-investments-and-omers-selling-associated-british-ports-stakes-to-ifm-investors">cp24.com</a></li>
        <li id="note-8"><cite>BNN Bloomberg</cite>, “CPP Investments selling Australian toll road assets for $4.5 billion,” 1 October 2026. <a href="https://www.bnnbloomberg.ca/business/company-news/2026/10/01/cpp-investments-selling-australian-toll-road-assets-for-45-billion/">bnnbloomberg.ca</a></li>
        <li id="note-9">CPP Investment Board, release of 15 August 2019, the purchase of 10.01% of 407 International for $3.0 billion, for a 50.01% stake (<a href="https://www.newswire.ca/news-releases/cppib-increases-investment-in-407-international-inc--879428070.html">newswire.ca</a>). PSP Investments, on the 2025 transactions: “Ferrovial at 48.29%, CPP Investments and other institutional investors at 44.20%, and PSP Investments at 7.51%” (<a href="https://www.investpsp.com/en/news/psp-investments-and-cpp-investments-complete-407-etr-transactions/">investpsp.com</a>).</li>
        <li id="note-10">PSP Investments, “AviAlliance completes acquisition of AGS Airports,” 28 January 2025: AviAlliance is “a wholly-owned subsidiary of PSP Investments”. <a href="https://www.investpsp.com/en/news/avialliance-completes-acquisition-of-ags-airports/">investpsp.com</a></li>
        <li id="note-11"><cite>The Globe and Mail</cite>, 15 July 2025: OMERS “owns around 32 per cent of Kemble”, Thames Water’s parent, and “wrote off the holding last year, which was once worth around $1-billion”. <a href="https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/article-thames-water-nationalization-165-billion-loss">theglobeandmail.com</a></li>
