        <li id="note-20">Department of Finance, “Canada Strong Fund,” 27 April 2026: “$25 billion over 3 years”; a retail product in which “initial invested capital will be protected” (<a href="https://www.canada.ca/en/department-finance/news/2026/04/canada-strong-fund.html">canada.ca</a>). <cite>Investment Executive</cite> (Canadian Press), on CPP Investments and Brookfield’s $50 billion fund, 15 September 2026 (<a href="https://www.investmentexecutive.com/news/industry/cpp-investments-brookfield-launch-50b-fund-to-invest-in-big-canadian-projects/">investmentexecutive.com</a>). Ontario Teachers’, “an additional $10 billion by the end of 2027” (note 5). OMERS, “at least $10 billion in new investments in Canada … over the next five years” (<a href="https://www.omers.com/news/omers-earns-6-9-billion-in-the-first-six-months-of-2026">omers.com</a>).</li>
